{"baseRefName":"main","body":"## Complete classification\nThis gives the point spectrum and full Banach-operator spectrum of f ↦ f∘A on complex C(U), with the supremum norm, for U the closed unit ball of an arbitrary complex norm and ||A||≤1. The statement covers zero and nilpotent eigenvalues, nonzero strictly stable eigenvalues, and peripheral eigenvalues in every combination.\n\nThe key step shows that every unimodular eigenfunction factors through the peripheral spectral projection, which is itself a contractive norm limit of powers of A. The resulting reversible-ball calculation and stable/nilpotent decomposition close the mixed-case reverse inclusion explicitly left open in Küster's 2015 thesis. Previously known cases, including its nilpotent-only Proposition 3.1.7, are credited. Historical priority of the completed classification remains unconfirmed.\n\n## Independent validation\n- Separate adversarial AI review: PASS_COMPLETE_CLASSIFICATION\n- All 473 exact submitted controls replay byte-identically; 907 independent exact controls pass\n- Eight independent-review files include frozen proof and replay dependencies\n- Exact source hypotheses were checked against the full 2016 OWR contribution and full primary 2015 thesis\n\nSee unsolved_math_prioritization/attempts/30003052/README.md and CLASSIFICATION.md. The proof is unchanged from the reviewed frozen snapshot; its submission-time pending header is superseded by the completed report and release metadata. This is not human peer review. One substantive proof family was used. The coordinating task updates the queue row separately.\n","headRefName":"dot/math-30003052","headRefOid":"2ea84c5de45cb92783b5b55057af1f52590be6bf","isDraft":true,"mergeable":"UNKNOWN","number":91,"state":"OPEN","url":"https://github.com/AlecKriebel/Math/pull/91"}
